Subject: Looking Forward to Volunteering at Tugman State Park

Hi, Franki,

Hope you're enjoying the holidays!

With my family far away, I didn=92t have plans myself, so I made an impulsi=
ve trip to Tugman State Park to check out the campground. I briefly met one=
 of the park rangers (I believe it was John) to make sure it was okay.

I didn=92t stay long, but I walked all three loops, checked out the shower =
facilities, and explored the day-use area trail. It gave me a great sense o=
f the space and the opportunities ahead.

I wanted to share that I=92m eager to commit to volunteering for three mont=
hs, January through March, if you=92ll have me that long. I understand the =
first month is probationary, and I=92d love to demonstrate my fit for this =
role. While I=92m likely to move on after March to explore other opportunit=
ies heading north along the 101, I=92d love to return the following year as=
 part of a circuit.

These three months will allow me to fully transition into the nomadic lifes=
tyle I=92ve been adopting while contributing to the park. Having a steady r=
outine close to Coos Bay will be invaluable as I work through some logistic=
al challenges and embrace this chapter of my journey.

I=92m also starting to explore recreational opportunities in the area and a=
m curious about the dunes (and dune buggies!) as well as moderately difficu=
lt ocean trails. It looks like a beautiful spot to immerse myself in nature=
.

On a practical note, I wanted to check that my name placard will read "Sam"=
 and not "Robert" (I go by my middle name). Also, I noticed some tree debri=
s in Loop C during my visit=97I'd be happy to help clear that if it=92s sti=
ll there when I return.

Looking forward to meeting you in just over a week!

Best regards,
Sam


